## 3. Travel billing models

### Model A — Deposit and final balance

Suitable for bookings that require an initial deposit and one later payment.

```text
BOOKING CREATED
      |
      v
INITIAL DEPOSIT DUE
      |
      v
DEPOSIT PAID
      |
      v
BOOKING CONFIRMATION
      |
      v
FINAL BALANCE DUE
      |
      v
FINAL PAYMENT
      |
      v
TRAVEL / SERVICE FULFILLMENT
```

### Model B — Multiple installments

Suitable for higher-value packages booked well in advance.

```text
BOOKING CONFIRMED
       |
       v
DEPOSIT PAYMENT
       |
       v
INSTALLMENT 1
       |
       v
INSTALLMENT 2
       |
       v
FINAL BALANCE
       |
       v
TRAVEL / SERVICE FULFILLMENT
```

### Model C — Scheduled payment

Suitable for an agreed future payment date.

The merchant's booking system or agreed billing workflow must define the due date and payment obligation.

### Model D — Recurring travel membership

Suitable for a genuine recurring membership, such as a travel club or accommodation membership.

This may use a subscription model, subject to commercial and product validation.

Do not represent a finite booking installment schedule as an indefinite recurring subscription.

